{
  "_comment": "Independent local reporters whose stories appear in the Watchdog home feed (synced hourly by property/scripts/sync_local_news.mjs). Set enabled to false to remove a source everywhere at once. type is wordpress (api = the site's /wp-json/wp/v2), rss (feed = its RSS URL) or youtube (channelId = the UC... id; read through the YouTube Data API with the YOUTUBE_API_KEY secret). A story is placed by the reporter's own town labels (townsFrom: categories, tags, url (a town in the link path) or none), then by a town named in the headline (titleMatch) or, with matchDescription, the start of a video description, then defaultTowns. Names are matched within counties (\"all\" = statewide); labelTowns pins label or headline names to a municipality code. query adds WordPress filters, perPage lowers the page size for sites with very large posts, imageHosts allows a photo CDN, imageWidth asks a resizing CDN for that width, imageLookup wp-media swaps feed photos for card-sized copies from the site's media list, imageOriginal uses the upload behind a 150px feed thumbnail, pageParam/pageStep/noPaging describe how an RSS feed pages, maxPages and crawlDelaySec keep requests within the site's robots.txt.",
